oking more carefully - the instructions say \"如果无法确认 venue，使用 ACL ARR 1-5 分制\". The narrative guidance mentions AAAI but the paper itself doesn't specify a venue. The paper is anonymous (\"Anonymous\") with no venue header. It's 10 pages + references which could fit AAAI (7+1+supplementary) or ACL (8+unlimited references). \n\nThe paper format doesn't explicitly state a venue. The narrative guidance mentions AAAI. Let me search for AAAI 2026 reviewer guidelines to use their scoring rubric, since that appears to be the target venue based on context.\n\nNow I'll look up the AAAI guidelines and set up two reviewer agents to work through this in parallel.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32665,"cache_read_input_tokens":23282,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32665},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"891f265c-8c20-445c-964a-94d66c0b1d82","uuid":"659680b9-29e6-4566-b517-4cfa16373239"}
